      "requirements": [
        "Simple inlineable means string/no-substitution-template/numeric literals or keyword kinds. Identifier and BigIntLiteral are excluded.",
        "Find an existing generated assignment before visiting the source expression; peel all outer wrappers and the rightmost comma/comma-list path. This cache predicate excludes compound assignments.",
        "The ordinary post-visit predicate peels only PartiallyEmittedExpression, admits every assignment operator with a generated Identifier left side, and allocates only when shouldHoist is true.",
        "The computed-name identity can be requested by constructor initialization before its declaration is hoisted by the member-name evaluation owner.",
        "An uncached auto-accessor allocates its temporary before expression visitation; its temporary and assignment use the expression raw range. Getter and setter preserve separate updated name nodes."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "References to transformAutoAccessor cover its name/cache invariant; backing/redirector producer and result-visitor dispositions remain separate.",
        "Generated identity is checked through metadata, never a printable underscore prefix."
      ]
